What are probes?
 In simple terms, probes are mechanisms used to monitor applications and take corrective actions when needed.

 𝐇𝐞𝐚𝐥𝐭𝐡 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐛𝐞𝐬 𝐢𝐧 𝐊𝐮𝐛𝐞𝐫𝐧𝐞𝐭𝐞𝐬
 Kubernetes uses health probes to continuously monitor applications and ensure they are highly available and self-healing. If something goes wrong, probes help Kubernetes decide the right recovery action automatically.

⚡ Types of Health Probes:

𝐑𝐞𝐚𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐞𝐬𝐬 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐛𝐞 → Ensures the application is ready to serve traffic.

readinessProbe:
 httpGet:
  path: /ready
  port: 8080
 initialDelaySeconds: 5
 periodSeconds: 3

𝐋𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐧𝐞𝐬𝐬 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐛𝐞 → Restarts the application if it becomes unhealthy.

livenessProbe:
 httpGet:
  path: /healthz
  port: 8080
 initialDelaySeconds: 10
 periodSeconds: 5

𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐫𝐭𝐮𝐩 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐛𝐞 → Useful for applications that take longer to start, especially legacy ones.

startupProbe:
 httpGet:
  path: /startup
  port: 8080
 failureThreshold: 30
 periodSeconds: 10


👉 Health Check Methods:
HTTP, TCP, Command execution

With these probes in place, Kubernetes ensures your workloads stay reliable, resilient, and production-ready. 
